INSTRUCTIONS = r"""
1. Select an .xlsx or .xlsm workbook. **Inspect queries** opens Excel read-only with external links disabled and reports only load states supported by observed Excel connections/tables; incomplete mappings remain Unknown.
2. Add `.m` and `.pq` sources (`.m/.pq`). Sorting and filtering only change the view. Edit the Order column or drag rows to change execution order.
   Query name, source path, enabled state, load mode, and order are editable in the manager table.
3. Use bulk enable/disable and the selected-order action as needed. Dependency analysis is advisory and flags ambiguous M constructs.
4. Select a source and choose **Inspect / compare selected** to view its exact M diff. Editing only changes an in-memory buffer. **Save edited source copy** writes a separate file; the original source is untouched.
5. Inspect workbook queries, export selected/all formulas or a versioned hash-verified query package, or save/load a versioned profile. ZIP package import restores query names/order and verifies each formula hash. Profile paths are relative to the profile file when possible. Enabled source-root mappings show a preview and require approval; longest matching root wins and ambiguous ties are rejected. Unsupported modes/options are rejected instead of being silently substituted.
   Existing query definitions are compared by formula and reported as new, changed, unchanged, conflict, or unknown.
6. Review the preview. **Plan only** does not open Excel or write a workbook/backup. Otherwise choose Replace or Skip and confirm. Definition-only is the default. Connection-only, new worksheet, existing worksheet, and Data Model loads are enabled only after the corresponding disposable-workbook probe succeeds for this Office version/build. Worksheet and Data Model loads evaluate M and may contact external sources; the review dialog requires explicit confirmation. Existing load destinations are preserved on repeat imports only when the requested mapping matches; unsupported conversions fail closed.
   Query definition only and connection-only remain separate modes; importing a definition or connection does not execute the M code, while a worksheet/model load evaluates M as part of loading.
7. After inspecting workbook connections, use **Refresh selected…** or **Refresh all…** to execute refreshable Power Query connections. This requires a separate explicit confirmation because external sources may be contacted. Choose synchronous or Excel background mode, set a timeout, and keep the default-on backup unless there is a reason not to. Refresh runs on a staged workbook; only successful refresh, save, close, and file replacement are reported as complete. Definition-only queries are reported as skipped.

Use **Probe Excel capabilities** to test this Office version/build on a disposable temporary workbook before enabling additional load modes. The probe evaluates only its own inline static `#table` M expressions and does not contact an external data source or execute a user's query.

All Excel COM operations run on a worker thread in an owned hidden Excel process. Import works on a staged sibling workbook copy; final replacement happens only after Save, read-only reopen verification of formulas and selected loads, and concurrent-change checks. Synchronous load evaluation has a bounded timeout that targets only the owned Excel process. Use a disposable workbook until your exact Excel build and workbook types pass the manual QA matrix.
""".strip()
